            <div xml:id="d5">

                <pb facs="0072" n="7" xml:id="pg7"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.90H/54: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Straus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-03-26T12:00:00+00:00">March 26,
                        1936—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received March 26—9 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>257. Department’s 98, March 23, 4 p.m. With textual alterations suggested by
                    Department provisional agreement with Afghanistan was signed by Ali Mohammed
                    Khan, Minister of the Kingdom of Afghanistan in London, and me at the Chancery
                    this morning at 11 o’clock.</p>
                <p>The signed instrument will be forwarded by next pouch.</p>
                <p>Repeat to Moscow.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Straus</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of the agreement, see Department of State Executive Agreement
                        Series No. 88, or 49 Stat. 3873.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
